From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:43:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma: add USB, with its PHYs and
 the PMU

On a normal boot ABL leaves the eUSB2 PHY off, so a bare DWC3 fails
its core soft reset (no UTMI clock). Describe the USB control block and
the eUSB2 PHY, with the PMU for PHY isolation, hand the DWC3 its
usb2-phy, and enable all three on husky in peripheral mode.

zuma has no clock driver yet. ABL leaves CMU_HSI0 running (the DWC3 ID
register reads back correctly), so a 19.2 MHz fixed clock stands in for
its USB clocks: the PHY drivers need a handle and the reference rate.
The eUSB2 PHY's supplies come from the PMIC, which has no driver yet
either, so they are left out and the driver runs on dummy regulators.
The eUSB2 repeater on I2C works as ABL leaves it.

Tested on a Pixel 8 Pro: the host enumerates the CDC NCM + ACM gadget
at high speed, and ssh over it works.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts     | 12 ++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi   | 58 +++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
index c9d34fb72..0e94b7b12 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
@@ -50,3 +50,15 @@ chosen {
 		 */
 	};
 };
+
+&usb_dwc3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_hsphy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usbdrd_phy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi
index e14d431e6..99a321f76 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma.dtsi
@@ -199,6 +199,18 @@ ramoops@fd3ff000 {
 		bldr-log@fd800000 { reg = <0x0 0xfd800000 0x100000>; no-map; };
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Stand-in for CMU_HSI0's USB clocks until zuma has a clock driver.
+	 * ABL leaves HSI0 clocked (the DWC3 ID register reads back correctly);
+	 * the PHY drivers only need a handle and the 19.2 MHz reference rate.
+	 */
+	clk_usb_stub: clock-usb-stub {
+		compatible = "fixed-clock";
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
+		clock-frequency = <19200000>;
+		clock-output-names = "usb_stub";
+	};
+
 	soc: soc@0 {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 		#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -216,21 +228,57 @@ gic: interrupt-controller@10400000 {
 		};
 
 		/*
-		 * The DWC3 controller. Stock has it in peripheral mode behind
-		 * Google's exynos9-dwusb glue, with an eUSB2 PHY at 0x11100000
-		 * and a Samsung eUSB2 repeater on I2C (0x3e). ABL leaves both
-		 * set up from fastboot [I], so the first-light gate tries the
-		 * bare core without a PHY node; a PHY driver comes next.
+		 * USB control block: Exynos 2200's link registers, with the
+		 * eUSB2 PHY below as its high-speed PHY. The USB3/DP combo PHY
+		 * (0x11130000) is left alone; the link runs at high speed.
+		 */
+		usbdrd_phy: phy@11100000 {
+			compatible = "google,zuma-usb32drd-phy";
+			reg = <0x11100000 0x200>;
+			clocks = <&clk_usb_stub>;
+			clock-names = "phy";
+			#phy-cells = <1>;
+			phys = <&usb_hsphy>;
+			phy-names = "hs";
+			samsung,pmu-syscon = <&pmu_system_controller>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		/* Synopsys eUSB2 PHY, the same IP and register map as Exynos 2200's. */
+		usb_hsphy: phy@11110000 {
+			compatible = "google,zuma-eusb2-phy",
+				     "samsung,exynos2200-eusb2-phy";
+			reg = <0x11110000 0x200>;
+			clocks = <&clk_usb_stub>, <&clk_usb_stub>, <&clk_usb_stub>;
+			clock-names = "ref", "bus", "ctrl";
+			#phy-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * The DWC3 controller, in peripheral mode as on stock (which
+		 * wraps it in Google's exynos9-dwusb glue). On a normal boot
+		 * ABL leaves the eUSB2 PHY off, so the core's soft reset only
+		 * completes once the PHY above supplies its UTMI clock. The
+		 * Samsung eUSB2 repeater on I2C (0x3e) has no driver yet.
 		 */
 		usb_dwc3: usb@11210000 {
 			compatible = "snps,dwc3";
 			reg = <0x11210000 0x10000>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 402 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			phys = <&usbdrd_phy 0>;
+			phy-names = "usb2-phy";
 			dr_mode = "peripheral";
 			maximum-speed = "high-speed";
 			snps,dis_u2_susphy_quirk;
 			snps,dis_u3_susphy_quirk;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
+
+		/* Writes go through EL3 (SMC), as on gs101. */
+		pmu_system_controller: system-controller@15460000 {
+			compatible = "google,zuma-pmu";
+			reg = <0x15460000 0x10000>;
+		};
 	};
 };
